  ],
  "notes": "Expected results are what the TypeScript gate returns: patterns compiled by RE2 with the rules file's flags (\"i\"). Python ports must compile with re.IGNORECASE | re.ASCII, use fullmatch for statusOnly patterns (search for obligation and noReplyKnown), and consume already-normalized text. The TypeScript normalizer replaces lone surrogates, applies NFC, truncates, then trims. Do not re-normalize, because JS String.prototype.trim and Python str.strip remove different character sets. re.ASCII makes \\b ASCII-only, as RE2's is ('sendé the file' matches the request lead), and stops re.IGNORECASE from folding dotless and dotted i to i ('nıce' is not 'nice'). One difference remains: RE2 case-folds U+017F (long s) to s, which re.ASCII does not, so a port must map U+017F to s before matching ('ſend the file' is an obligation). NFC already rewrites the other such character, U+212A (Kelvin sign), to K."
}
